1)  Don't screw up at Sokoban ;-).  No, seriously, try to think 
    ahead a bit before pushing boulders.  You might even use some 
    props like bread crumbs on a paper map to envisage what's going 
    on if that's helping.  

2)  Until you're confident to solve Sokoban, don't go there without 
    some backup which helps you out (useful tools include wands of 
    striking and teleport, pickaxes and mallocks).  

3)  If you blocked the exit or are stuck somehow, check if 

        (a) teleporting a boulder is helpful (if possible), 
        (b) it's worth to destroy a boulder (be careful with 
            the range of striking wands/spells, however).  

    If both options are not possible, there is a last chance:  Strip 
    down naked and squeeze under the boulder.  Your stuff is not 
    necessarily lost; you can throw it.  
    
